ising every admissible \\(k\\)**  \n\n   *\\(k=0\\).*  \n   Use the \\(n\\) horizontal lines \\(y=1,\\dots ,y=n\\).  All are non\u2011sunny and every\n   \\((a,b)\\in T_n\\) lies on the line \\(y=b\\).\n\n   *\\(k=1\\).*  \n   Take the \\(n-1\\) horizontal lines \\(y=1,\\dots ,y=n-1\\) and the sunny line\n   \\[\n   \\ell_{\\text{sun}}:\\;y=(1-n)x+2n-1 ,\n   \\]\n   which passes through \\((1,n)\\) and \\((2,1)\\).  The horizontal lines cover all points with second coordinate \\(\\le n-1\\); the remaining point \\((1,n)\\) lies on \\(\\ell_{\\text{sun}}\\).\n\n   *Even \\(n\\) and \\(k=n-1\\).*  \n   Write \\(n=2m\\;(m\\ge2)\\).  \n   \u2013 **Non\u2011sunny line:** the diagonal \\(D:x+y=2m+1\\) (slope \\(-1\\)).  \n   \u2013 **Sunny lines:** for each \\(r\\in\\{1,2,\\dots ,2m-1\\}\\) define  \n\n     \\[\n     \\ell_r:\\;y=\\frac{r-2m}{\\,r-1\\,}x+\\frac{2m}{\\,r-1\\,}.\n     \\tag{6}\n     \\]\n\n     The line \\(\\ell_r\\) passes through the two points \\((r,1)\\) and \\((1,2m+1-r)\\); its slope\n     \\(\\frac{r-2m}{r-1}\\) is never \\(0,\\infty,-1\\), so \\(\\ell_r\\) is sunny.\n     \n     **Coverage check.**  \n     Let \\((a,b)\\in T_{2m}\\) and set \\(r:=a+b-1\\) (so \\(1\\le r\\le2m-1\\)).  \n     Substituting \\(a,b\\) into (6) gives  \n\n     \\[\n     b=\\frac{r-2m}{r-1}a+\\frac{2m}{r-1}\n     \\Longleftrightarrow (r-1)b=(r-2m)a+2m .\n     \\]\n\n     Using \\(r=a+b-1\\) the right\u2011hand side simplifies to \\((a+b-1-2m)a+2m\\),\n     which equals \\((r-2m)a+2m\\); the equality holds, so \\((a,b)\\) lies on \\(\\ell_r\\).\n     Hence every point of \\(T_{2m}\\) with sum \\(a+b\\le2m\\) lies on exactly one of the\n     sunny lines \\(\\ell_r\\); the points with sum \\(2m+1\\) lie on the diagonal \\(D\\).\n     Consequently the family \\(\\{D\\}\\cup\\{\\ell_r\\}_{r=1}^{2m-1}\\) consists of\n     \\(2m=n\\) distinct lines, exactly \\(n-1\\) of which are sunny, and covers all points of \\(T_n\\).\n\n   *Odd \\(n\\) and arbitrary \\(k\\) ( \\(0\\le k\\le 