\\) lines be sunny.\n   By Lemma\u202f1 each sunny line contributes at most\n   \\(\\displaystyle f:=\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor\\) points,\n   while a non\u2011sunny line (horizontal, vertical or of slope \\(-1\\))\n   contains at most \\(n\\) points of \\(T_{n}\\).\n   Consequently\n   \\[\n   kf+(n-k)n\\ge |T_{n}|=\\frac{n(n+1)}2 .\n   \\tag{5}\n   \\]\n   Solving (5) gives the sharp upper bound  \n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\n   k\\le\n   \\begin{cases}\n   n-1,& n\\text{ even},\\\\[2mm]\n   n,  & n\\text{ odd}.\n   \\end{cases}}\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Maximal\u2011\\(k\\) constructions.**  \n   We prove that the bound (6) is attainable.\n\n   *Even \\(n=2m\\) (maximal \\(k=n-1\\)).*  \n   Define the following \\(n\\) distinct lines.\n\n   *Sunny lines* (there are \\(n-1=2m-1\\) of them):\n   \\[\n   L_{t}:\\;y=x+t\\qquad\n   t=-(m-1),-(m-2),\\dots ,0,\\dots ,m-1 .\n   \\tag{7}\n   \\]\n   (All have slope \\(1\\), hence are sunny.)\n\n   *One non\u2011sunny line*: the vertical line\n   \\[\n   V:\\;x=m .\n   \\tag{8}\n   \\]\n\n   **Verification that every point of \\(T_{2m}\\) lies on one of the lines.**  \n   Let \\((a,b)\\in T_{2m}\\) and put \\(t=b-a\\).\n\n   *Case\u202f1 \u2013 \\(t\\le 0\\).*  \n   Then \\(t\\) belongs to the set \\(\\{-(m-1),\\dots ,0\\}\\) because\n   \\(a\\ge1,\\;b\\ge1\\) and \\(a+b\\le2m+1\\) imply\n   \\[\n   -(m-1)\\le b-a\\le0 .\n   \\]\n   Hence \\((a,b)\\) lies on the sunny line \\(L_{t}\\).\n\n   *Case\u202f2 \u2013 \\(t>0\\).*  \n   From \\(a+b\\le2m+1\\) we obtain \\(a\\le 2m+1-b = 2m+1-(a+t)\\),\n   i.e. \\(2a\\le 2m+1-t\\).  Since \\(t\\ge1\\), we have \\(2a\\le2m\\) and\n   therefore \\(a\\le m\\).  Consequently the point belongs to the vertical\n   line \\(V\\) (which contains all points with first coordinate \\(m\\)).\n   \u220e\n\n   The construction uses exactly \\(2m-1=n-1\\) sunny lines, proving that the\n   bound is attainable for even \\(n\\).\n\n   *Odd \\(n=2m-1\\) (maximal \\(k=n\\)).*  \n   Again